hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15486","Musa ibn Tariq Abu Qurrah al-Zubaydi narrated to us, of the people of al-Husayb, and beside it is Rima, and it is the village of Abu Musa al-Ashari, my father said: And Abu Qurrah was a judge for them in Yemen. He said: Ayman ibn Nabil Abu Imran narrated to us, he said: I heard a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), called Qudamah, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stone Jamrat al-Aqabah on the day of sacrifice."
"15487","Abu Qurrah said: And Sufyan al-Thawri added in this hadith of Ayman: On a reddish she-camel, without driving, nor beating, nor away, away."
"15488","Waki narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, he said: I heard an old man of Banu Kilab called Qudamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Ammar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of sacrifice stoning the jamrah on a reddish she-camel of his, no striking, nor driving, nor away, away."
"15489","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, Qudamah ibn Abd Allah al-Kilabi narrated to us that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stone the jamrah, the Jamrat al-Aqabah, from the belly of the valley on the day of sacrifice, on a reddish she-camel of his, no striking, nor driving, nor away, away."
"15490","Qurran said in the hadith: He stones the jimar on a she-camel of his."
"15491","Abd Allah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus and Muhriz ibn Awn ibn Abi Awn Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, both said: Qurran ibn Tammam al-Asadi narrated to us, Ayman narrated to us, from Qudamah ibn Abd Allah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a she-camel touching the Stone with his cane."
"15492","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhriz ibn Awn and Abbad ibn Musa narrated to me, both said: Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Ayman ibn Nabil, from Qudamah ibn Abd Allah, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the jimar on a she-camel, no striking, nor driving, nor away, away. And Abbad added in his hadith, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a reddish she-camel stoning the jamrah."
"15493","Mutamir narrated to us, from Ayman ibn Nabil, from Qudamah ibn Abd Allah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of sacrifice stoning the jamrah on a reddish she-camel of his, no striking, nor driving, nor away, away."
